 ## Project Root Resolution
 
-Before reading any repo-relative path, derive `PROJECT_ROOT` from this loaded `SKILL.md`: start at the skill file's directory and walk upward until the nearest directory containing both `AGENTS.md` and `modes/`. This is required even when the checkout itself is nested (for example `Development\\career-ops`) or the command starts from a subdirectory. If those two sentinels cannot be found, stop and locate the career-ops checkout before reading or writing files. Then derive `DATA_ROOT`, where the user's own files live, with the precedence `path-resolver.mjs` uses: `CAREER_OPS_ROOT` or `CAREER_OPS_DATA_DIR` if either is set; otherwise the path written in `PROJECT_ROOT/.career-ops-data` if that file exists and is not empty; otherwise `PROJECT_ROOT` itself. A relative value in either place resolves against `PROJECT_ROOT`. Run from `PROJECT_ROOT`, `node -e "import('./path-resolver.mjs').then(m => console.log(m.getCareerOpsRoot()))"` prints the same directory. With no override the two roots are one directory.
+Before reading any repo-relative path, derive `PROJECT_ROOT` from this loaded `SKILL.md`: start at the skill file's directory and walk upward until the nearest directory containing both `AGENTS.md` and `modes/`. This is required even when the checkout itself is nested (for example `Development\\career-ops`) or the command starts from a subdirectory. If those two sentinels cannot be found, stop and locate the career-ops checkout before reading or writing files. Then derive `DATA_ROOT`, where the user's own files live, with the precedence `path-resolver.mjs` uses: `CAREER_OPS_ROOT` or `CAREER_OPS_DATA_DIR` if either is set; otherwise the path written in `PROJECT_ROOT/.career-ops-data` if that file exists and is not empty; otherwise `PROJECT_ROOT` itself. A relative value in either place resolves against `PROJECT_ROOT`. When `PROJECT_ROOT` is a Claude Code plugin install (its path contains `/.claude/plugins/cache/`), the plugin cache is replaced on every plugin update, so the codebase root is never the default `DATA_ROOT` there: with neither the environment variables nor the marker set, `DATA_ROOT` is `~/career-ops` (create it if missing). Before running any script from a plugin install, run `npm install` in `PROJECT_ROOT` if `PROJECT_ROOT/node_modules` is missing; modes that drive a browser also need `npx playwright install chromium` once. A plugin install does not load `AGENTS.md` as project context, so read `PROJECT_ROOT/AGENTS.md` once per session before running any mode and follow it; its Update Check does not apply there, since the plugin updates through `/plugin`. Run from `PROJECT_ROOT`, `node -e "import('./path-resolver.mjs').then(m => console.log(m.getCareerOpsRoot()))"` prints the same directory. With no override the two roots are one directory.
 
 Resolve every path in this router against one of these two roots, never against the process's current working directory. User Layer paths resolve against `DATA_ROOT`. They include `cv.md`, `article-digest.md`, `portals.yml`, `config/` (except the shipped `*.example.*` files), `data/`, `reports/`, `output/`, `interview-prep/`, `modes/_profile.md`, `modes/_custom.md`, `modes/_brief.md`, `batch/tracker-additions/`, and every other User Layer path in `DATA_CONTRACT.md`. Everything else (the other `modes/` files, scripts, templates, the `config/*.example.*` files) resolves against `PROJECT_ROOT`.
 
diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
